    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Cruz LLC Medical Group**\n\n**Patient:** Catherine Day \n**DOB:** 12/28/1955 \n**Sex:** F \n**MRN:** 392115 \n\n**Encounters:**\n- **2024-11-10:** \n Patient presented for follow-up of breast cancer, stage I. Blood pressure was 138/89, and weight was 161 pounds. \n Exam: Vital signs within normal limits. HEENT exam unremarkable. Cardiovascular exam showed normal S1 and with no murmurs, gallops, or rubs. Respiratory exam with clear breath sounds bilaterally. Abdominal exam soft and non-tender. Extremities with no edema. Neurological exam non-focal. Minor skin rash noted on the left forearm, no other dermatological concerns. \n- **2023-03-21:** \n Patient presented for follow-up of breast cancer, stage I. Blood pressure was 139/96, and weight was I73 pounds. \n Exam: Vital signs within normal limits. HEENT exam unremarkable. Cardiovascular exam showed normal S1 and S2 with no murmurs, gallops, or rubs. Respiratory exam with clear breath sounds bilaterally. Abdominal exam soft and non-tender. Extremities with no edema. Neurological exam non-focal. Patient complained of mild, intermittent headache. \n- **2021-07-29:** \n Patient presented for follow-up of breast cancer, stage I. Blood pressure was 129/88, and weight was 166 pounds. \n Exam: Vital signs within normal limits. HEENT exam unremarkable. Cardiovascular exam showed normal S1 and S2 with no murmurs, gallops, or rubs. Respiratory exam with clear breath sounds bilaterally. Abdominal exam soft and non-tender. Extremities with no edema. Neurological exam non-focal. Patient reported experiencing occasional joint pain, which is not of concern.\n\n**Assessment/Plan:**\n- **Breast cancer, stage I (status post treatment approximately 0.7 years ago) - active;** \n Medications: anastrozole 1 mg daily. \n Note: The patient has been non-compliant with medications and missed two scheduled follow-up appointments. Continued education and reinforcement of adherence to her medication regimen is necessary. \n- **Tobacco use:** \n Former smoker of cigarettes at a rate of one per day, quit on May 5, \n- **Alcohol use:** \n Patient reports consuming approximately ten alcoholic drinks per week. \n\n**Social History:**\n- The patient has a family history of myocardial infarction in her father, who diagnosed at age 66. He passed away before we could gather more details on his condition. \n\n**Conclusion:**\nThe patient continues to manage her stage I breast cancer with prescribed anastrozole. Non-compliance with her medication and missed appointments remain a concern, necessitating ongoing i"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "ntervention and support. Her cardiovascular risk factors include elevated blood pressure readings at recent visits, which should be monitored closely. Additional history of tobacco use and alcohol consumption should also be considered in her overall health assessment.\n\n---\n\n**Dr. Robert Carroll** \n**Oncology** \n**Cruz LLC Medical Group**\n"
    }
